# Small lookup tables for Rudvalis transition certificates, part 6

These tables split the published ATLAS permutation data into blocks of 64
images. Kernel-checked equality with the original generator actions makes
word evaluation through these tables a sound alternative for the dense
level-0 transition checks, avoiding large intermediate packed integers.

Source: `PermutationData` and `OrderChainData`, as documented in
`OrderCertificate/GenerateChain.g`. Generated by `GenerateLevel0Part6Tables.py`;
the Python computation only supplies witnesses.
